# octet npm launcher

`@skaft/octet` is a small Node.js launcher for the native octet runtime. npm
selects one exact-version platform package through `optionalDependencies`; the
`octet` and `octet-host` commands start the selected native binary directly.

These scoped names are source packaging identities, not proof of registry rights
or availability. Use the installation command only after an authorized release
has published the packages.

The launcher requires Node.js but does not access the network, download an
archive, or execute an install lifecycle hook. Install it with scripts, audit,
and funding requests disabled:

```sh
npm install --global --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund @skaft/octet@VERSION
```

GNU/Linux uses the glibc x64 package. macOS uses the arm64 or x64 package that
matches the running executable. `octet doctor` reports a missing `rg`
prerequisite.
